        "path": "_m/w/9/4/9/mari-mari-cultural-village-wp/hero.jpg",
        "filename": "Mari Mari Cultural Village entrance (11949663055).jpg",
        "caption": "The next halt and the last halt for the day was the Mari Mari Cultural village. Seen here is the entrance hut and ticket office of the park, set in the fading evening light. The village, is actually a theme park of sorts which introduces you to various traditional homes of Sabahan ethnic communities—the Bajau, Lundayeh, Murut, Rungus and Dusun—which are built by descendants of the tribes which they represent. (Kota Kinabalu, East Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
